#
# Conformance case: explanation/transitive-derivation
# AC: explanation — faithfulness gate passes for transitively derived fact.
#
# A three-term subOf chain: A subOf B, B subOf C in world-main.
# The transitivity rule derives A subOf C. The explanation for this derived
# quad must cite ONLY IRIs present in the proof trace: the rule IRI, the
# reifier IRIs for both premises, the term IRIs A, B, C, and subOf.
# The runner's assert_explanation_faithful gate must pass for every quad.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/explanation/transitive-derivation/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: three Kinds in a linear subOf hierarchy
ex:A a logic:Kind .
ex:B a logic:Kind .
ex:C a logic:Kind .

# Rule: transitivity of ex:subOf
# ?X subOf ?Y  AND  ?Y subOf ?Z  =>  ?X subOf ?Z
ex:ruleTransitiveSubOf a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleTransitiveSubOf ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?X" ;
        rdf:predicate ex:subOf ;
        rdf:object    "?Z"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?X" ;
        rdf:predicate ex:subOf ;
        rdf:object    "?Y"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?Y" ;
        rdf:predicate ex:subOf ;
        rdf:object    "?Z"
    ] .
